    "title": "Stephen A. Smith Wants To Manage Roman Reigns - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Clark ,\n46 minutes ago\nStephen A. Smith continues to flirt with the idea of stepping into the WWE spotlight, and he already knows exactly who he’d want by his side if that ever became a reality.\nThe ESPN personality has spent the past several weeks joking about becoming a WWE heel, and during a recent episode of his podcast featuring Danhausen, the conversation turned toward the possibility of managing a WWE Superstar.\nREAD MORE: John Cena – ‘The Only Person Who Could Convince Me To Come Back Is Elon Musk’\nREAD MORE: ‘The Duke Of Dorchester’ Pete Doherty Passes Away\nWhen asked whether he had ever considered taking on a manager role, Smith admitted that the idea has crossed his mind. He said,\n“I’ve thought about doing the heel manager thing. Should I do it?”\nDanhausen then asked who he would choose to represent if given the opportunity. Smith didn’t hesitate with his answer. He said,\n“I don’t know. Roman Reigns… Maybe. I acknowledge him. He’s big time…I wouldn’t have somebody that’s small time.”\nNOTE: If you have any news tips or podcast recaps that you’d like to send in for us to post (full credit will be given to you), please email me at RClarkPWS@Yahoo.com .",
    "summary": "Stephen A. Smith continues to flirt with the idea of stepping into the WWE spotlight, and he already knows exactly who he’d want by his side if that ever became a reality. The ESPN personality has spent the past several weeks joking about becoming a WWE heel, and during a recent episode of his podcast featuring Danhausen, the conversation turned toward the possibility of managing a WWE Superstar.",
